WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.029
Hey guys, it's Jan here.
Part of the fun of a new Pixar movie is spotting

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:09.139
all the Easter Eggs and references that the
animators have cleverly packed into the film.

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.440
So, I'm happy to say that the studio's latest
flick, The Good Dinosaur, has plenty to keep

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.480
us Easter Egg-hunters entertained!
With the movie out now, I've collected as

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.900
many eggs and references as I could spot in
this video.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.730
I know your eagle eyes will have noticed other
fab ones too, so share away in the comments

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.460
below!
Just a quick reminder there are spoilers ahead,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:33.090
so if you're not ready for that, check out
my non-spoiler review of the movie right here!

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.840
After eating some rotten fruit they found
on the ground, Arlo and Spot start laughing

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.550
and hallucinating. As well as floating through
the air and swapping heads with each other,

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.180
they also see multiple eyes pop up on each
other's faces, giving them a look similar

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.670
to "Squishy" aka Scott Squibbles, a character
in Monsters University, who just happens to

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.199
have been voiced by The Good Dinosaur director
Peter Sohn!

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:59.500
Oh, and by the way, The Good Dinosaur was
originally meant to be released before Inside

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.010
Out and after Monsters University; so it's
no surprise that Monsters University had a

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:08.200
little Easter Egg for this movie in the shape
of a toy Arlo on a bedroom floor.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.490
Of course, Arlo and Spot aren't the first
animated characters who've been drunk or under

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.549
the influence of other, er, substances! For
example, in Disney's Dumbo, Dumbo and Timothy

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:22.729
Q Mouse get drunk on champagne and start hallucinating
pink and multi-coloured elephants. And, more

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:27.520
recently, in Big Hero 6 Baymax behaves like
he's drunk when he's low on battery.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.310
When the Styracosaurus Forrest Woodbush and
Arlo compete to see who gets to keep the little

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.119
pooch-like human, they have a naming match,
with each of them suggesting names. One of

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.799
the name's Arlo comes up with is Spike, which
also happens to be the name of the slug-like

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:48.100
employee Augustus Jones at Monsters, Inc!
And, interestingly, Spike was also the real

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:53.750
name of the dog who played Old Yeller in the
classic 1957 Disney movie, which director

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.740
Peter Sohn has said was an influence on The
Good Dinosaur.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:01.060
Oh, and I think I also heard Arlo suggest
the name Grumpy, who of course is one of the

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.390
seven dwarves in Disney's Snow White And The
Seven Dwarves!

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.709
When Arlo and Spot are running away from a
bunch of pterodactyls, they see what looks

00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:12.629
like the silhouette of an adult Apatosaurus
in the distance, which is an easter egg for

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:17.200
the Dinoco sign in Toy Story, although as
they get closer they see the silhouette is

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.660
actually made up of two T-rexes.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:24.360
The Good Dinosaur also has a whole bunch of
easter eggs to the Jurassic Park movies.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:29.129
When Arlo and Spot duck down behind a rock
in the middle of a plain as a herd of longhorns

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:33.709
run around them, it's a definite call-back
to the scene in Jurassic Park where the Gallimimus

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:38.060
run through the valley as a flock, and Dr
Grant and the kids hide behind a tree trunk.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.730
And when Spot tries to hide inside a tree
trunk from the pterodactyls trying to attack

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.790
him, it calls to mind when Julianne Moore
hid in a tree trunk from a stegosaurus in

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:51.519
The Lost World and Omar Sy hid inside a tree
trunk from a raptor in Jurassic World.

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:55.700
Also, there's also a little Lion King reference
in the scene where three raptors approach

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.989
Arlo and Spot, ready to attack them, which
feels very similar to when the trio of hyenas

00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:03.760
did the same to Simba and Nala.
But there's actually a fourth raptor in The

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.140
Good Dinosaur; and just like the scenes in
Jurassic Park where raptors are shown working

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:12.700
together, one of them distracting you, while
another attacks you from a different side;

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.300
three raptors take Arlo and Spot's attention
from the front, while a fourth one tries to

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.129
pounce on them from the back.
Oh, and the raptor who sneaks up on Arlo from

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:26.159
behind is called Earl and he's voiced by none
other than Pixar's lucky charm himself, John

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:29.470
Ratzenberger.
And when the raptors jump on Butch's back

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.560
and attack him, it calls to mind the scene
in Jurassic Park where the raptor attacks

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:38.269
the T-rex in the Visitors' Centre.
When two raptors go to attack Arlo, T-rex

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:43.319
steps in and saves him by scooping them up
in his jaws and tossing them away, just like

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:48.069
at the end of Jurassic Park.
And when the T-rexes and Arlo roar after defeating

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:52.970
the raptors, it's a nice nod to the T-rex's
roar at the end of Jurassic Park and Jurassic

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:55.379
World.
Oh, and by the way, the scenes with Arlo and

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:59.530
the chickens are a reminder that birds are
the closest modern-day descendants of dinosaurs.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.860
And they're also a nod to palaeontologist
Jack Horner who consulted on all the Jurassic

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:09.049
Park movies and whose research focuses on
dinosaur evolution and includes reverse-evolving

00:04:09.049 --> 00:04:13.099
a dinosaur from a chicken.
And on another dinosaur-related point, I kind

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:16.949
of felt like the asteroid belt at the start
of the movie resembled a dinosaur skeleton

00:04:16.949 --> 00:04:21.549
with a long tail, with one of the asteroids
looking like a dinosaur skull.

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:26.581
The phrase 'the storm provides', which Thunderclap,
the pterodactyls' leader, says over and over,

00:04:26.581 --> 00:04:30.270
has a definite ring of the line 'the Dude
abides' from The Coen Brothers' movie The

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.860
Big Lebowski, which as well as starring Jeff
Bridges in the lead as Jeffrey "The Dude"

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.300
Lebowski, also featured actor Sam Elliott,
who's the voice of Butch the T-rex in The

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.300
Good Dinosaur.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.600
And there's a nice nod to the movie Jaws when
the pterodactyls return later, and we see

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.570
the bottom bit of their wings sticking out
from beneath the clouds, like up-side-down

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:51.389
shark fins!
And given that Jaws is one of the favourite

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:55.410
films of The Good Dinosaur director Peter
Sohn, it's no wonder that there's another

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.759
Jaws reference in the movie too. The scene
where the T-rexes sit round the campfire at

00:04:59.759 --> 00:05:03.550
night swapping tales of how they got their
battle-scars is really reminiscent of the

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.900
scene in Jaws where Richard Dreyfuss and Robert
Shaw's characters Hooper and Quint do the

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:08.900
same.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.380
Oh, and could this be an ancestor of the blue-footed
protagonist of the lead character in Pixar's

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.160
cancelled feature film Newt?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.330
I was looking for a Finding Dory Easter Egg
and I noticed a rock formation that looked

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:23.300
rather like Crush, the sea turtle from Finding
Nemo. And although I don't think Crush will

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:27.130
be a major part of Finding Dory, wouldn't
it be awesome if he had a little cameo in

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.919
the film! By the way, in the rocks just above
Crush, it looks like there's the image of

00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:35.740
a sloth, which could be a shout out to Flash
the sloth from Disney's next animation Zootopia?

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:41.530
Now, you'll be wondering where the regular
Pixar easter eggs like A113, the Luxo Ball,

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:46.759
and the Pizza Planet Truck are. As you can
imagine in a movie set almost entirely outdoors

00:05:46.759 --> 00:05:50.580
during the prehistoric era when there was
no modern-day writing, toys or machinery,

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:55.770
these easter eggs don't seem to be anywhere
obvious, so I think the filmmakers have used

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.430
creative techniques to include them in the
film.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:03.910
I found a possible A113 easter egg in the
gopher scene. When Arlo goes to blow a gopher

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:08.729
out of its hole for the first time, a single
gopher emerges slowly and the shape it makes

00:06:08.729 --> 00:06:13.979
is a bit like an A. Then Spot blows out 2
more gophers, one on either side of him which

00:06:13.979 --> 00:06:19.160
could indicate a "one" and another "one".
And then Arlo blows out 3 gophers sitting

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:23.389
on top of each other, which, of course is
the "3". All of which adds up to A-1-1-3!

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:28.090
Another possibility is the stick scene where
Arlo puts out 5 sticks each one representing

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:33.210
one member of his family. The A in this case
would be A for Arlo, one-one would be the

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:37.910
first 2 sticks, his mother and father, and
three would be the last 3 sticks which are

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.860
their three children.
So there you have my best theories at the

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:45.960
moment for possible A113 easter eggs. Let
me know what you think and if you spotted

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.880
it anywhere else in the movie.
I didn't see an obvious Luxo ball, but look

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:54.270
carefully at this shot of the sun in the sky
above the T-rexes and you'll see a big blue

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:59.259
ring of light around the sun with the sun
itself representing the star in the Luxo ball.

00:06:59.259 --> 00:07:03.919
And in this close-up shot of red berries,
there seems to a five-pointed star shape in

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:08.300
the white reflection on some of the berries.
I also scoured the film for the pizza planet

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.440
truck. The closest I've found so far is this
cloud formation which as far as cloud formations

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:18.490
go, doesn't feel like a normal-looking cloud.
The shape is a little blocky, a bit like the

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:23.560
pizza planet truck and there's a dark blob
on top which might suggest the rocket.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:28.780
I was hoping to see A113, the Luxo ball, and
pizza planet perhaps on a rock carving somewhere

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:33.330
but I didn't spot them. Let me know if you
noticed them anywhere else or if you've got

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:36.960
any theories on where they're hidden!
And what about the tree with the berries that

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:41.880
Spot takes Arlo to? It seems to have some
similarities to the Pixar tree which we first

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.879
saw in A Bug's Life and later in Toy Story
2 and Up.

00:07:44.879 --> 00:07:49.449
So, guys, what other Easter Eggs and references
did you see in The Good Dinosaur? And which

